      "id": "9c994805eaa4-q1",
      "number": 1,
      "question": "In 1812, who described the hypothesis that equal volumes of different gases contain an equal number of molecules? 1812 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2351;&#2361; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2341;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2327;&#2376;&#2360;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2339;&#2369; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In 1812, who described the hypothesis that equal volumes of different gases contain an equal number of molecules?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>1812 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2351;&#2361; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2341;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2327;&#2376;&#2360;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2339;&#2369; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Amedeo Avogadro &#2309;&#2350;&#2375;&#2342;&#2367;&#2323; &#2309;&#2357;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Amedeo Avogadro</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2350;&#2375;&#2342;&#2367;&#2323; &#2309;&#2357;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "James Watt &#2332;&#2375;&#2350;&#2381;&#2360; &#2357;&#2377;&#2335;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">James Watt</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2332;&#2375;&#2350;&#2381;&#2360; &#2357;&#2377;&#2335;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "John Dalton &#2332;&#2377;&#2344; &#2337;&#2366;&#2354;&#2381;&#2335;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">John Dalton</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2332;&#2377;&#2344; &#2337;&#2366;&#2354;&#2381;&#2335;&#2344;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Albert Einstein &#2309;&#2354;&#2381;&#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335; &#2310;&#2311;&#2306;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2368;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Albert Einstein</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2354;&#2381;&#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335; &#2310;&#2311;&#2306;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2368;&#2344;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p>&#183; In <b>1812</b>, <b>Amedeo Avogadro</b>, an Italian scientist, proposed the <b>Avogadro's hypothesis (or Avogadro's law)</b>, which states that <b>equal volumes of different gases, at the same temperature and pressure, contain an equal number of molecules</b>. </p><p>&#183; This foundational principle later became crucial in the development of the <b>kinetic theory of gases</b> and modern chemistry.</p><p>Why not the others?</p><p>&#183; <b>James Watt</b>: A Scottish inventor known for improving the steam engine, unrelated to gas laws.</p><p>&#183; <b>John Dalton</b>: Proposed <b>Dalton's atomic theory</b> but did not formulate Avogadro's hypothesis.</p><p>&#183; <b>Albert Einstein</b>: Worked on Brownian motion and quantum theory, much later (early 20th century).</p><p><b>Fun Fact:</b> Avogadro's number (6.022  X  10&#178;&ge; molecules/mol) was named in his honor, though it was determined after his lifetime.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "9c994805eaa4-q2",
      "number": 2,
      "question": "For which discovery did Henri Becquerel receive the Nobel Prize in Physics in 1903? &#2361;&#2375;&#2344;&#2352;&#2368; &#2348;&#2375;&#2325;&#2381;&#2357;&#2375;&#2352;&#2375;&#2354; &#2325;&#2379; 1903 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2326;&#2379;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2349;&#2380;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2379;&#2348;&#2375;&#2354; &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>For which discovery did Henri Becquerel receive the Nobel Prize in Physics in 1903?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2361;&#2375;&#2344;&#2352;&#2368; &#2348;&#2375;&#2325;&#2381;&#2357;&#2375;&#2352;&#2375;&#2354; &#2325;&#2379; 1903 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2326;&#2379;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2349;&#2380;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2379;&#2348;&#2375;&#2354; &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;?</span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Spontaneous Radioactivity &#2360;&#2381;&#2357;&#2340;&#2307;&#2360;&#2381;&#2347;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340; &#2352;&#2375;&#2337;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2343;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340;&#2366;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Spontaneous Radioactivity</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2381;&#2357;&#2340;&#2307;&#2360;&#2381;&#2347;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340; &#2352;&#2375;&#2337;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2343;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340;&#2366;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Radioactive Elements &#2352;&#2375;&#2337;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2343;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2368; &#2340;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Radioactive Elements</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2375;&#2337;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2343;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2368; &#2340;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Radium Emanation &#2352;&#2375;&#2337;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2360;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Radium Emanation</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2375;&#2337;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2360;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2344;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Diagnostic Radiography &#2337;&#2366;&#2351;&#2327;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2375;&#2337;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2347;&#2368;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Diagnostic Radiography</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2337;&#2366;&#2351;&#2327;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2375;&#2337;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2347;&#2368;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p>Henri Becquerel shared the 1903 Nobel Prize in Physics with Marie and Pierre Curie for his discovery of spontaneous radioactivity in uranium in 1896.</p><p>This groundbreaking discovery was made somewhat accidentally when Becquerel observed that uranium salts had fogged a photographic plate without exposure to sunlight, demonstrating natural radiation emission.</p>",
