      "id": "9c994805eaa4-q3",
      "number": 3,
      "question": "In which year did Robert Brown observe the zigzag movement of colloidal particles in solution? &#2352;&#2377;&#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335; &#2348;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2313;&#2344; &#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2357;&#2367;&#2354;&#2351;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337;&#2354; &#2325;&#2339;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2335;&#2375;&#2338;&#2364;&#2368;-&#2350;&#2375;&#2338;&#2364;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2342;&#2375;&#2326;&#2368; &#2341;&#2368;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In which year did Robert Brown observe the zigzag movement of colloidal particles in solution?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2377;&#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335; &#2348;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2313;&#2344; &#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2357;&#2367;&#2354;&#2351;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337;&#2354; &#2325;&#2339;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2335;&#2375;&#2338;&#2364;&#2368;-&#2350;&#2375;&#2338;&#2364;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2342;&#2375;&#2326;&#2368; &#2341;&#2368;?</span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "1829 1829",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">1829</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1829</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "1826 1826",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">1826</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1826</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "1828 1828",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">1828</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1828</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "1827 1827",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">1827</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1827</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>Robert Brown, a Scottish botanist, first observed the zigzag (random) movement of colloidal particles in 1827 while studying pollen grains suspended in water under a microscope. This motion, later called Brownian motion, was explained by Albert Einstein in 1905, confirming that it results from the collision of particles with molecules of the surrounding medium.</p>",
