      "number": 4,
      "question": "Which type of electromagnetic radiation was discovered by Johann Wilhelm Ritter in 1801? &#2332;&#2379;&#2361;&#2366;&#2344; &#2357;&#2367;&#2354;&#2381;&#2361;&#2375;&#2350; &#2352;&#2367;&#2335;&#2352; &#2344;&#2375; 1801 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2340; &#2330;&#2369;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2325;&#2368;&#2351; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2367;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2368; &#2326;&#2379;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2341;&#2368;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which type of electromagnetic radiation was discovered by Johann Wilhelm Ritter in 1801?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2332;&#2379;&#2361;&#2366;&#2344; &#2357;&#2367;&#2354;&#2381;&#2361;&#2375;&#2350; &#2352;&#2367;&#2335;&#2352; &#2344;&#2375; 1801 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2340; &#2330;&#2369;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2325;&#2368;&#2351; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2367;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2368; &#2326;&#2379;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2341;&#2368;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "X-rays &#2319;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;-&#2352;&#2375;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">X-rays</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;-&#2352;&#2375;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Ultraviolet rays &#2346;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2376;&#2306;&#2327;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2352;&#2339;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Ultraviolet rays</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2346;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2376;&#2306;&#2327;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2352;&#2339;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Infrared rays &#2309;&#2357;&#2352;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2352;&#2339;&#2375;&#2306;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Infrared rays</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2357;&#2352;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2352;&#2339;&#2375;&#2306;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Gamma rays &#2327;&#2366;&#2350;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2352;&#2339;&#2375;&#2306;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Gamma rays</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2327;&#2366;&#2350;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2352;&#2339;&#2375;&#2306;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p>&bull; <b>Johann Wilhelm Ritter</b>, a German physicist, discovered <b>ultraviolet (UV) rays</b> in <b>1801</b>.</p><p>&bull; He noticed that invisible rays just beyond the violet end of the visible spectrum caused <b>silver chloride</b> to darken quickly.</p><p>&bull; This discovery confirmed the existence of radiation beyond violet light, hence the term <b>\"ultra-violet\"</b>.</p><p><b>Other Options:</b></p><p>&bull; <b>X-rays</b>  -  Discovered by <b>Wilhelm Conrad R&#246;ntgen</b> in <b>1895</b>.</p><p>&bull; <b>Infrared rays</b>  -  Discovered by <b>William Herschel</b> in <b>1800</b> (just a year before Ritter's discovery).</p><p>&bull; <b>Gamma rays</b>  -  Discovered by <b>Paul Villard</b> in <b>1900</b>.</p>",
