        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "CV Raman &#2360;&#2368; &#2357;&#2368; &#2352;&#2350;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">CV Raman</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2368; &#2357;&#2368; &#2352;&#2350;&#2344;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "SN Bose &#2319;&#2360; &#2319;&#2344; &#2348;&#2379;&#2360;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">SN Bose</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2360; &#2319;&#2344; &#2348;&#2379;&#2360;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "John Tyndall &#2332;&#2377;&#2344; &#2335;&#2367;&#2306;&#2337;&#2354;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">John Tyndall</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2332;&#2377;&#2344; &#2335;&#2367;&#2306;&#2337;&#2354;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p>At this institute, <b>Sir C. V. Raman</b> discovered in 1928 that when a beam of coloured light entered a liquid, a fraction of the light scattered by that liquid was of a different color. Raman showed that the nature of this scattered light was dependent on the type of sample present.</p>",
