      "id": "9c994805eaa4-q7",
      "number": 7,
      "question": "In which year did Galileo describe the regular, swinging motion of a pendulum by the action of gravity and acquired momentum? &#2327;&#2376;&#2354;&#2368;&#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379; &#2344;&#2375; &#2327;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2339; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2357;&#2375;&#2327; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2346;&#2375;&#2306;&#2337;&#2369;&#2354;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340;, &#2333;&#2370;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In which year did Galileo describe the regular, swinging motion of a pendulum by the action of gravity and acquired momentum?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2327;&#2376;&#2354;&#2368;&#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379; &#2344;&#2375; &#2327;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2339; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2357;&#2375;&#2327; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2346;&#2375;&#2306;&#2337;&#2369;&#2354;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340;, &#2333;&#2370;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "1605 1605",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">1605</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1605</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "1600 1600",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">1600</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1600</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "1599 1599",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">1599</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1599</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "1602 1602",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">1602</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1602</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>&#183; <b>Galileo Galilei</b> first described the <b>regular swinging motion of a pendulum</b> in <b>1602</b> after observing a chandelier in Pisa Cathedral.</p><p>&#183; He discovered that the <b>period of oscillation</b> (time of swing) was constant and depended on the <b>length of the pendulum</b>, not the amplitude.</p><p>&#183; This laid the foundation for <b>pendulum clocks</b> (later developed by Christiaan Huygens in 1656).</p>",
      "images": [],
