    {
      "id": "9c994805eaa4-q8",
      "number": 8,
      "question": "Who propounded the famous equation E = mc&#178; in 1905? 1905 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2360;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; E = mc&#178; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Who propounded the famous equation E = mc&#178; in 1905?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>1905 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2360;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; E = mc&#178; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Werner Heisenberg &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2344;&#2352; &#2361;&#2366;&#2311;&#2332;&#2375;&#2344;&#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Werner Heisenberg</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2344;&#2352; &#2361;&#2366;&#2311;&#2332;&#2375;&#2344;&#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Isaac Newton &#2310;&#2311;&#2332;&#2364;&#2376;&#2325; &#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2335;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Isaac Newton</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2310;&#2311;&#2332;&#2364;&#2376;&#2325; &#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2335;&#2344;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Albert Einstein &#2309;&#2354;&#2381;&#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335; &#2310;&#2311;&#2306;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2368;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Albert Einstein</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2354;&#2381;&#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335; &#2310;&#2311;&#2306;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2368;&#2344;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Ernest Rutherford &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2344;&#2375;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335; &#2352;&#2342;&#2352;&#2347;&#2379;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Ernest Rutherford</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2344;&#2375;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335; &#2352;&#2342;&#2352;&#2347;&#2379;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>The famous equation <b>E = mc&#178;</b> was propounded by <b>Albert Einstein</b> in <b>1905</b> as part of his theory of <b>Special Relativity</b>.</p><p>&#183; <b>E</b> stands for energy.</p><p>&#183; <b>m</b> stands for mass.</p><p>&#183; <b>c&#178;</b> is the square of the speed of light (which is approximately <b>3  X  10&#8312; m/s</b>).</p><p>This equation shows that energy (<b>E</b>) and mass (<b>m</b>) are interchangeable, with the speed of light (<b>c</b>) as the constant of proportionality.</p><p>It fundamentally changed our understanding of physics and paved the way for advancements in nuclear energy and quantum mechanics.</p><p><b>Further insights:</b></p><p>&#183; Heisenberg was a <b>German physicist</b> and one of the key figures in the development of <b>quantum mechanics</b>. He is most famous for the <b>Heisenberg Uncertainty Principle</b>, which states that it is impossible to precisely measure both the position and momentum of a particle at the same time.</p><p>&#183; Newton was an <b>English mathematician and physicist</b> and is considered one of the most influential scientists in history. He formulated the <b>laws of motion</b> and <b>universal gravitation</b>.</p><p>&#183; Rutherford was a <b>New Zealand-born British physicist</b> known for his work on the structure of the <b>atom</b>. He is best known for discovering the <b>nucleus</b> and his model of the atom, and for his work on radioactivity.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "9c994805eaa4-q9",
      "number": 9,
      "question": "Who discovered the atomic number based on X-ray wavelength in 1913? 1913 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;-&#2352;&#2375; &#2340;&#2352;&#2306;&#2327;&#2342;&#2376;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352;&#2350;&#2366;&#2339;&#2369; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2326;&#2379;&#2332; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Who discovered the atomic number based on X-ray wavelength in 1913?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1913 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;-&#2352;&#2375; &#2340;&#2352;&#2306;&#2327;&#2342;&#2376;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352;&#2350;&#2366;&#2339;&#2369; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2326;&#2379;&#2332; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368;?</span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "A.E.B. de Chancourtois &#2319;.&#2312;.&#2348;&#2368;. &#2337;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2344;&#2325;&#2379;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335;&#2379;&#2311;&#2360;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">A.E.B. de Chancourtois</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;.&#2312;.&#2348;&#2368;. &#2337;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2344;&#2325;&#2379;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335;&#2379;&#2311;&#2360;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Dmitri Mendeleev &#2342;&#2367;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;&#2337;&#2375;&#2354;&#2368;&#2357;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Dmitri Mendeleev</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2342;&#2367;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;&#2337;&#2375;&#2354;&#2368;&#2357;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Henry Moseley &#2361;&#2375;&#2344;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2379;&#2360;&#2354;&#2368;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Henry Moseley</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2361;&#2375;&#2344;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2379;&#2360;&#2354;&#2368;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "R.A. Millikan &#2310;&#2352;.&#2319;. &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2367;&#2325;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">R.A. Millikan</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2310;&#2352;.&#2319;. &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2367;&#2325;&#2344;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>In 1913, Henry Moseley, an English physicist, discovered that the atomic number (Z) of an element is directly related to its X-ray wavelength.</p><p>&#183; Moseley's Experiment: </p><p>o He used X-ray spectroscopy to study elements and arranged them in increasing atomic number rather than atomic mass.</p><p>o This resolved inconsistencies in Mendeleev's Periodic Table (which was based on atomic mass).</p><p>o His discovery led to the modern periodic law: </p><p>&#167; \"The properties of elements are periodic functions of their atomic numbers.\"</p><p>Thus, the correct answer is Henry Moseley.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
